     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I want to estimate franciscana (<i>Pontoporia blainvillei</i>) bycatch for six different\r\nareas. The model was structured as follow:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">                                                                       <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">formulaM3=y~0+Intercept+area+offset(LogRede)+f(s,model=spde)+f(Year,model=&quot;iid&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">M3=inla(formulaM3,family=&quot;Poisson&quot;,data=inla.stack.data(stk.est),control.compute=list(dic=TRUE),\r\ncontrol.predictor=(list(A=inla.stack.A(stk.est))))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">My question\r\nis: How I do the prediction of franciscana bycatch for each area? </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">sim &lt;-\r\nfranciscanafit$sims.matrix<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>area1</sub>&lt;-\r\n1/(1+exp(-sim[,1]))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>area2</sub>\r\n&lt;- 1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,2])))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>Area3 </sub>&lt;-\r\n1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,3])))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>Area4 </sub>&lt;-\r\n1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,4])))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>Area5 </sub>&lt;-\r\n1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,5])))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">y<sub>Area6 </sub>&lt;-\r\n1/(1+exp(-(sim[,1]+sim[,6])))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">The above code is just to give some idea that what\r\nI want to do. In the above code I have only one covariate (area) using\r\nR2winbugs package. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">After the prediction of franciscana bycatch for\r\neach area, the total bycatch would be obtained multiplying by the total fishery\r\neffort.  <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:black;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
